            "review_text": "marioJkt25\nDepok, Indonesia485 contributions\n0\nRather be an overpriced one, IMHO.\nFeb 2020 • Friends\nFrankly, I would say this restaurant is overpriced. But it's a halal one. For the price of 80K VND, I could get a big bowl of beef noodle with plenty of beef on it outside, instead of a plate of flat taste and dull fried rice here. The Vietnamese spring rolls is okay, with quite proper size for 80K. Their milk coffee ice is okay, but slightly more expensive rather than other restaurants (30K), and their Tea O (20K) was came in a small cup without a tea bag, so it is impossible for you to ask for additional hot water. This restaurant could be your option if you have an extra money, but for me, once is enough.\nRead more\nWritten February 2, 2020",
