            "review_text": "The British Asian Backpacker\nAccrington, United Kingdom111 contributions\n2\nAlhamdulillah 🙏🏽\nFeb 2019 • Solo\nThis restaurant was located on a street with many other Halal restaurants. I couldn't tell if it was open at first but then I could see the open sign in the door.\n\nI walked in and noticed many other local Muslims indicating the food was good. There was a slight smell of fish.\n\nI was greeted warmly by the owner who gave us menus and left us to browse. The prices were slightly more expensive than non-Halal restaurants and it was Malay food. I ordered a chicken curry and rice for 105,000 VD (£3.47). I was kindly given a free Mirinda soft drink. \n\nThe food arrived quickly and was average. The curry was a little cold and there wasn't much chicken.\n\nOn a side note, neither me nor my friend were differently even though we were dressed in shorts and t-shirts. \n\nI would only recommend this restaurant based on the Halal options and the service!\nRead more\nWritten February 23, 2019",
