            "review_text": "Cindy Soka\nMelbourne, Australia354 contributions\n1\nA lacklustre lunch\nFeb 2019 • Solo\nI went to Hjh Basiroh Hj Aku today for lunch. The restaurant’s door was closed so I initially thought it was closed, but they close the door because there is air con in there.\n\nThe restaurant was reasonably busy when I arrived. I felt welcome and comfortable dining there even though I am not Muslim.\n\nThe restaurant serves Malaysian and Vietnamese food with most dishes under 90,000VD (£3).\n\nI ordered stir fried noodles with prawns for 90,000 VD. I was asked if I wanted them spicy - I confirmed.\n\nMy food arrived within 10 minutes. It’s presentation wasn’t anything to write home about. \n\nI noted that I only had three big prawns in the noodles. I would have liked at least two more. Unfortunately, I didn’t enjoy the food. I thought there was a strange bitter taste to it and wasn’t spicy at all. Apart from that there were not herbs or spices used to add flavour. \n\nThe gentleman who served me was very welcoming. He asked where I was from and also let me refill my 1.5l water bottle.\nRead more\nWritten February 22, 2019",
